{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_3febb772-e751-48f3-aa69-79e624d6f678","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_9340cc673b32c591","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8/20260915T161838Z-ba2694ea/runs/specialist/f008270e09ad48e7afc9b262b3aacada\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\nLOG_B=\"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8/20260915T161838Z-ba2694ea/runs/baseline/614857fe763a4e2a821ef61850b1e81e/benchmark_vllm_20260915_171250/server.log\"\nLOG_P=\"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8/20260915T161838Z-ba2694ea/reports/enablement/9d27140cf07749878ef698ad2789b20d/server.log\"\nSRC=\"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm\"\n\nswitches=[{\n \"switch\":\"VLLM_GFX90A_FP8_EMULATION\",\n \"category\":\"(e) swap an operator implementation for a vendor kernel / (f) keep a tensor resident on the device\",\n \"target\":\"vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/scaled_mm/emulation.py: FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel.is_supported / process_weights_after_loading ; registered in vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/__init__.py: _POSSIBLE_FP8_KERNELS[ROCM] and _LINEAR_BACKEND_KERNEL_MAP['emulation']\",\n \"evidence\":f\"{LOG_B}:52 'Selected ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel for CompressedTensorsW8A8Fp8' -> {LOG_B}:229+ RuntimeError 'torch._scaled_mm is only supported on CUDA devices with compute capability >= 9.0 or 8.9, or ROCm MI300+' in all 8 TP workers during gpu_model_runner.profile_run\",\n \"default\":\"off (unset -> is_supported() returns False, selection byte-for-byte the original)\",\n \"depends_on\":[],\n \"enables\":[\"VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE\"],\n \"notes\":\"enabling this switch alone does not boot the engine: the rewrite changes which kernel the traced dense linears lower to, so the previously saved AOT graph must not be replayed. See VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE.\"}]\npatch=\"patches/001_gfx90a_fp8_emulation_defaultoff.patch\"\n\np1={\"name\":\"gfx90a-fp8-emulation-armed+fresh-compile\",\n \"args_mode\":\"append\",\"atomic\":True,\"extra_args\":\"\",\n \"extra_envs\":{\"VLLM_GFX90A_FP8_EMULATION\":\"1\",\"VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE\":\"1\"},\n \"reason\":\"Two-part enablement, benched as one variant. (1) The patch adds a default-OFF FP8 w8a8 dense-linear kernel that dequantizes the FP8 weight to BF16 ONCE at load time and then runs plain F.linear, replacing the ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel that vLLM currently selects on gfx90a and that dies in torch._scaled_mm (MI250X/CDNA2 has no FP8 MMA and reports a spoofed capability (9,0), so the Torch kernels' own arch gate never fires). (2) VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1 is co-required: the server replays a hash-keyed AOT artifact (decorators.py:543-563) whose hash covers only config + model source, NOT the kernel registry, and _verify_source_unchanged only re-checks files the OLD artifact traced - so a selection-changing patch never invalidates it. The 17:05 patched boot logged 'Directly load AOT compilation from .../63eba2e7...' and then died on that stale graph's guard assert_size_stride(arg10_1,(4096,2560),(1,4096)) against the now-BF16 [2560,4096] weight: the artifact, not the patch, is what is incompatible. Split them and each half is dead - the switch alone hits the stale graph, and a fresh compile without the switch reproduces the baseline scaled_mm abort.\",\n \"kb_evidence\":[],\n \"pr_evidence\":[],\n \"source_evidence\":[f\"{SRC}/model_executor/kernels/linear/__init__.py:407-415 (_POSSIBLE_FP8_KERNELS[ROCM] priority list, patched kernel inserted ahead of the three Torch kernels)\",\n   f\"{SRC}/compilation/decorators.py:523-563 + :295-311 (AOT hash dir, 'Directly load AOT compilation', _verify_source_unchanged)\",\n   f\"{SRC}/envs.py:158,354,1404 (VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE)\",\n   f\"{LOG_B}:52,229-300\",f\"{LOG_P}:53,362-381,589,1844\",\"patches/001_gfx90a_fp8_emulation_defaultoff.patch\"]}\n\np2={\"name\":\"fp8-emulation-via-linear-backend-triton+fresh-compile\",\n \"args_mode\":\"append\",\"atomic\":True,\n \"extra_args\":\"--linear-backend triton\",\n \"extra_envs\":{\"VLLM_GFX90A_FP8_EMULATION\":\"1\",\"VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE\":\"1\"},\n \"reason\":\"Variant of P1 that makes the rewrite reach the MoE expert GEMMs too, which is the residual risk in P1. --linear-backend filters the SCALED-MM registry only and falls back to normal selection with a warning for every layer type the backend has no kernel for (kernels/linear/__init__.py:596-628 _resolve_backend_kernels), so it does not touch the TRITON Fp8 MoE backend already selected at server.log:54; what it does change is the dense side: with both the emulation kernel and the Triton FP8 w8a8 kernel in the triton bucket, the arch-gated emulation kernel still wins on gfx90a and the dequant stays a one-time load-time event instead of a per-step weight cast. Cost: dense GEMMs leave the BF16-native path, which on CDNA2 is the fastest available, so this is expected to measure at or below P1 - its value is as a correctness probe on the hypothesis that a MoE/block-wise FP8 path is a second blocker behind the compile cache.\",\n \"kb_evidence\":[],\"pr_evidence\":[],\n \"source_evidence\":[f\"{SRC}/model_executor/kernels/linear/__init__.py:596-628,648-660 (--linear-backend filtering + first-fit selection)\",\n   f\"{SRC}/config/kernel.py:142-237 (LinearBackend literals incl. 'triton', 'emulation')\",\n   f\"{LOG_B}:52-54 (dense = ChannelWiseTorch..., MoE = TRITON Fp8 backend)\"]}\n\np3={\"name\":\"no-patch-fresh-compile-probe\",\n \"args_mode\":\"append\",\"atomic\":False,\"extra_args\":\"\",\n \"extra_envs\":{\"VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE\":\"1\"},\n \"reason\":\"Cheap discriminator to run if P1 is not adopted, and the only proposal that needs no source change: it re-benches the ALREADY-INTEGRATED (advanced, task 684650cc) gfx90a emulation patch on the current baseline with the stale AOT artifact ruled out. If the engine boots, the patch was never the problem and the whole 17:10 'expected size 2560==4096' failure is confirmed as cache replay; if it still dies, the next error is a genuine second gap and its traceback is what a following round needs. Zero risk to the sealed baseline (switch unset => identical selection), and it is strictly cheaper than P1 because it needs no integrate step.\",\n \"kb_evidence\":[],\"pr_evidence\":[],\n \"source_evidence\":[f\"{LOG_P}:53 (patched tree does select FP8W8A8EmulationLinearKernel)\",\n   f\"{LOG_P}:362-381 ('Directly load AOT compilation from path /root/.cache/vllm/torch_compile_cache/torch_aot_compile/63eba2e7...')\",\n   f\"{LOG_P}:589,1844 (assert_size_stride(arg10_1,(4096,2560),(1,4096)) from inside that cached artifact)\",\n   f\"{SRC}/compilation/caching.py:_verify_source_unchanged\"]}\n\nfindings=[\n {\"what\":\"vLLM 0.28's AOT compile cache does not invalidate on kernel-SELECTION changes, so any enablement patch to the scaled_mm registry is unreproducible on a host with a warm /root/.cache/vllm. The AOT dir hash covers config factors + _model_hash_key(forward) only (decorators.py:537-546), and on load _verify_source_unchanged re-checks only the traced files recorded by the EXISTING artifact - a patch that only edits the registry __init__ and adds a new kernel module changes neither, so the pre-patch graph (which hard-codes extern_kernels._scaled_mm on an FP8 [K,N] column-major weight) is replayed against a now-BF16 [N,K] row-major weight and dies on inductor's arg guard, not on the patch.\",\n  \"source\":f\"{LOG_P}:362-381 + :589 + :1844; {SRC}/compilation/decorators.py:295-311,523-563\",\"expected_impact\":\"Converts the currently dead baseline into a booting server; without it every future kernel-selection enablement patch will appear to fail for the wrong reason.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none (build-cache correctness)\",\"domain_tags\":[\"vllm\",\"torch.compile\",\"aot-cache\",\"enablement\",\"mi250x\"]},\n {\"what\":\"On gfx90a the FP8 registry selects ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel and aborts, because gfx90a reports compute capability (9,0) and the Torch scaled_mm kernels gate on 'capability >= 89'. The aiter FP8 kernels above it are correctly arch-gated off, so the first kernel that passes is one that cannot run. This is an engine-level failure independent of TP / concurrency / params, and no existing --quantization or --linear-backend value can avoid it on this checkpoint: 'emulation' maps only to MXFP4/6/8 and NVFP4 kernels, 'torch' maps exactly to the three aborting kernels, and 'triton' has no entry in _LINEAR_BACKEND_KERNEL_MAP so it warns and falls back.\",\n  \"source\":f\"{LOG_B}:52 + :229-300; {SRC}/model_executor/kernels/linear/__init__.py:296-340,407-415; {SRC}/model_executor/kernels/linear/scaled_mm/pytorch.py:227\",\"expected_impact\":\"Explains why the gap is un-closable by config alone and why a source patch is mandatory.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none\",\"domain_tags\":[\"vllm\",\"rocm\",\"gfx90a\",\"fp8\",\"kernel-selection\"]},\n {\"what\":\"The gfx90a dequant path is cheap: the dense FP8 weight volume rewritten per TP rank is only ~0.29 GiB -> ~0.59 GiB BF16 (server.log 'So far 0.29 GiB of FP8 weights -> 0.59 GiB'), i.e. the 397B model's expert weights keep their own TRITON Fp8 MoE backend and never touch the emulation kernel. Memory headroom is therefore not the constraint; and because the dequant happens inside process_weights_after_loading it is a load-time event, not per-step work.\",\n  \"source\":f\"{LOG_P}:192-211 + :54 (MoE backend selected separately)\",\"expected_impact\":\"Bounds the downside risk of P1/P2 and says the residual gap after boot is the MoE side, not the dense side.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"low - the E4M3->BF16 cast is exact, and the activation is no longer requantized to FP8, which removes one error term versus a true w8a8 scaled GEMM.\",\"domain_tags\":[\"vllm\",\"memory\",\"moe\",\"fp8\"]}]\n\nqs=[\"Does integrate_patch install into /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm (where the console script /opt/venv/bin/vllm resolves) or into /opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm? The two trees are distinct, and the baseline server.log shows no emulation.py log lines even in the run whose patch was status=advanced - so either the patch never reached the serving interpreter, or that log predates the install. If the patch is not landing, proposals P1/P2 must be re-targeted before benchmarking.\",\n \"Is /root/.cache/vllm/torch_compile_cache shared/persistent across Hyperloom sessions on this host? If it persists between the baseline and the patched leg, every kernel-selection variant this session measures is confounded, and the coordinator may want VLLM_CACHE_ROOT pointed at a per-run directory instead of VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1 (which also costs a full compile, roughly the 4-minute load-to-first-token gap seen at 17:05 -> 17:09).\",\n \"For the record: does the accuracy gate accept the BF16-dequant w8a8 path (activation stays BF16, no FP8 requant) as within band for this checkpoint, or should a future round target the Triton FP8 w8a8 path for the dense linears to match reference numerics more closely?\",\n \"MoE side is the predicted next blocker: fp8.py selects TRITON Fp8 MoE on gfx90a with block-wise scales - confirm from a fresh boot whether the expert GEMMs actually execute (they never got to run in either observed failure).\"]\n\npayload={\"intent_type\":\"specialist_done\",\"payload\":{\n \"confidence\":0.7,\"domain\":\"framework_rewrite_specialist\",\"empty\":False,\n \"gap_canonical_id\":\"inference:ornith-1.5-397b-fp8:mi250x:vllm:qwen3_5_moe:qwen3_5moeforconditionalgeneration:0.28.0:fp8#fail:baseline:subprocess_nonzero\",\n \"summary\":\"Localized why the baseline is still dead and shipped a default-OFF rewrite. Two distinct causes, one patch plus one co-required env: (1) on gfx90a the FP8 registry selects ChannelWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel - capability spoofing makes its >=89 gate pass - and torch._scaled_mm aborts; a new dequant-at-load BF16 kernel fixes that and is gated off unless VLLM_GFX90A_FP8_EMULATION=1. (2) vLLM replays a hash-keyed AOT compile artifact that a selection-only patch cannot invalidate, which is exactly what produced the 17:10 'expected size 2560==4096' shape assert on the patched tree - so VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1 is declared as a dependent lever. 3 variants, 1 patch.\",\n \"patches_written\":[patch],\n \"framework_switches\":switches,\n \"proposal_set\":[p1,p2,p3],\n \"new_findings\":findings,\n \"residual_questions\":qs,\n \"artifacts_written\":[]}}\njson.dump(payload,open(\"specialist_done.partial.json.tmp\",\"w\"),indent=1)\nos.replace(\"specialist_done.partial.json.tmp\",\"specialist_done.partial.json\")\nprint(\"partial ok; json valid:\",bool(json.load(open(\"specialist_done.partial.json\"))))\nPY\necho \"elapsed $(( $(date -u +%s) - $(date -u -d 2026-09-15T17:41:51Z +%s) ))s/600\"","description":"Write full checkpoint payload"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd537a3d-60c1-464c-91c7-bfdb763c2d0f","uuid":"538442db-298b-4dd0-b157-42b92d1ca6f3"}
